    "scope": "36 normal/sanitized export checks of the full signed 32-bit result: all 256 byte inputs at seven constants and all 65536 word inputs at two constants for each function. Each distinct QASM circuit is independently sparsely simulated; identical exports reuse the same simulation. Input phases, negative-result phases and all private-wire zeros are checked. GCC sanitizer flags can preserve subtraction where the ordinary frontend folds addition of a negative constant, so circuit identity is not required. No-table export; O2 and builtin mode only. Sparse simulation covers this logical H/X/phase export subset with terminal observations, not arbitrary dense or channel circuits.",
    "basis_scope": "Every basis path in each selected circuit is checked separately after verifying canonical uniform H preparation followed exclusively by reversible X/phase gates. Labels prevent an input permutation from hiding behind uniform amplitudes. Complete signed 32-bit results, preserved inputs, phases and zero private wires are checked for fresh zero ancillas. This is finite circuit evidence for the listed metadata/input domains, not arbitrary C correctness."
  },
